<LegalLayout
  title="About Drawinging"
  description="Learn about Drawinging’s educational purpose, tutorial structure, and worksheet approach."
  permalink="/about/"
>
  <p>
    Drawinging is an educational drawing tutorial website. We publish step-by-step lessons, category collections, and
    printable worksheets so learners can practise with clear sequences—not with an online drawing tool or account-based
    studio.
  </p>
  <h2>What we publish</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Subject tutorials with materials, steps, tips, and FAQs</li>
    <li>Category hubs for browsing related lessons</li>
    <li>Drawing fundamentals guides</li>
    <li>Downloadable PDF and SVG worksheets</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>How tutorials are structured</h2>
  <p>
    Each lesson starts with construction shapes, moves through numbered steps, then covers refinement, common mistakes,
    and a practice worksheet. Content is written to be subject-specific rather than templated filler.
  </p>
  <h2>Images and updates</h2>
  <p>
    Tutorial images begin as labeled placeholders at final production paths. When final illustrations are ready, they
    replace the same filenames. Pages show published and updated dates so learners can see when a lesson last changed.
  </p>
  <h2>Honesty standards</h2>
  <p>
    We do not invent user counts, awards, expert credentials, or ratings. Educational claims stay limited to what the
    page actually teaches.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
